From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 00:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] guid: cache a machine-id GUID fallback when Common.UUID absent

RAKP messages 2 and 4 must carry the 16-byte Managed System GUID, which
getSystemGUID() reads from xyz.openbmc_project.Common.UUID over D-Bus.
On platforms with no UUID provider (e.g. TiogaPass) that read throws and
the canned fallback was returned WITHOUT being cached, so the blocking,
failing ObjectMapper lookup re-ran on every single RAKP message (twice
per session). On the single-core AST2500 this synchronous failing lookup
starves netipmid's single-threaded event loop, so concurrent logins under
a polling IPMI monitor see their RAKP packets answered late or not at all
("no response from RAKP 1/3", intermittent session failures).

Derive a deterministic GUID from /etc/machine-id (matching the in-band
Get System GUID handler's app-id) and cache it, so the failing lookup runs
at most once. The registered GUID-change callback still overrides the cache
if a real UUID later appears on D-Bus.
---
 command/guid.cpp | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/command/guid.cpp b/command/guid.cpp
index a963f02..1a3c38a 100644
--- a/command/guid.cpp
+++ b/command/guid.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 #include <phosphor-logging/lg2.hpp>
 #include <xyz/openbmc_project/Common/error.hpp>
 
+#include <systemd/sd-id128.h>
+
 #include <sstream>
 #include <string>
 
@@ -87,8 +89,41 @@ const Guid& getSystemGUID()
     }
     catch (const sdbusplus::exception_t& e)
     {
-        lg2::error("Failed in reading BMC UUID property: {ERROR}", "ERROR", e);
-        return fakeGuid;
+        // No xyz.openbmc_project.Common.UUID provider on D-Bus (e.g. on
+        // TiogaPass).  Fall back to a deterministic machine-id-derived GUID
+        // and cache it, so this blocking, failing ObjectMapper lookup is not
+        // repeated on every RAKP message.  Repeating it stalls netipmid's
+        // single-threaded event loop and causes intermittent "no response from
+        // RAKP" session failures under polling load.  The already-registered
+        // GUID-change callback still overrides this cache if a real UUID later
+        // appears on D-Bus.  The same machine-id app-id is used by the in-band
+        // Get System GUID handler so both report the same value.
+        lg2::debug("BMC UUID absent on D-Bus, using machine-id fallback: "
+                   "{ERROR}",
+                   "ERROR", e);
+        static constexpr sd_id128_t bmcGuidAppId = SD_ID128_MAKE(
+            1f, 2e, 3d, 4c, 5b, 6a, 47, 89, a0, b1, c2, d3, e4, f5, 06, 17);
+        sd_id128_t machineGuid{};
+        char guidStr[SD_ID128_STRING_MAX];
+        if (sd_id128_get_machine_app_specific(bmcGuidAppId, &machineGuid) >= 0)
+        {
+            try
+            {
+                Guid tmpGuid{};
+                rfcToGuid(sd_id128_to_string(machineGuid, guidStr), tmpGuid);
+                guid = tmpGuid;
+                return guid.value();
+            }
+            catch (const InvalidArgument& ia)
+            {
+                lg2::error("Failed parsing machine-id GUID: {ERROR}", "ERROR",
+                           ia);
+            }
+        }
+        // Last-resort: cache the canned GUID so we still never repeat the
+        // failing lookup.
+        guid = fakeGuid;
+        return guid.value();
     }
 
     std::string rfc4122Uuid = std::get<std::string>(propValue);
